WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.223
Hi, I’m Kishi Bashi

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:16.224
And I’m Toby.

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:17.142
Hope you like our music.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.228
K and I love to play music

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.314
We had the chance to write music for Stillwater, this wonderful show.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:24.899
That's so much fun.

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:29.863
It allows me and Toby, you know, the composers to really, to have fun with music.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.749
And we really would hope that you would play some with us today, would that be okay?

00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:35.754
Would you like to try?

00:00:35.754 --> 00:00:37.287
Uhh, okay.

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:38.830
We brought our instruments.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.040
Got mine!

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:41.082
Did you guys bring yours?

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:44.753
Do you guys have your bowls and spoons? Toby, what do you think? Are they ready?

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:49.424
Let me see… yeah they, I don’t know… oh yeah, yeah. They got them.

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.593
Okay, well let’s make music together. Toby, you ready?

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:52.594
I'm ready.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:59.893
Okay, well let’s start with a beat. Okay so, you guys grab your bowl and spoon.
And tap along.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:03.980
And it’s okay if you don’t have one, you can also just clap like me, okay?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.858
So clap along ‘cause I’m going to start playing the violin. Ready?

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:07.859
Great job everybody!

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.527
One, two, three, four.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:55.698
Woo, that was fun!

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:57.075
That sounded awesome! Great job!

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:59.744
Wow, you guys did amazing! You guys are all musicians here.

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:06.960
Now, I have a question. How did that make you feel? Um, happy? Calm? Excited? Sad?

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:15.051
Music can make us feel lots of things. The type of music that I really enjoy sometimes is music that just invites you to feel.

00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:19.514
It just is this open invitation to experience something.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:23.977
I was about seven years old when I started the violin. And I think I loved it so much because it’s like singing.

00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:25.061
You know, it’s like…

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:31.609
*singing* na ta da… oooo.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:35.738
It’s kind of like, uh, it was really beautiful to me so I’ve played it ever since.

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:40.910
K and I actually went to school together, so we were growing up playing music together.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.788
Playing music with your friend is probably one of the best things you could ever do.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:48.668
There’s like one thing better than making music is making music with your friends. And that’s so much fun.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.295
Hey Toby, why don’t we play a game?

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:51.588
Sure, what are you, what are you thinking?

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:55.383
Let’s try to name a feeling and then make music to match it.

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:58.970
Interesting. Okay, let’s give it a try.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.265
Alright, well let’s start with the feeling of happiness. You ready?

00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:03.808
I’m ready. Let’s do it.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.102
You know, Toby, why don’t you kick it off?

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.021
One, two, three, four.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:39.427
I’m pretty happy.

00:03:39.427 --> 00:03:42.513
That melody really made me happy. Toby, what makes you happy about that?

00:03:42.513 --> 00:03:47.852
Yeah, the melody made me happy and um, the ukulele always makes me happy.

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:49.604
Yeah, I like, the ukulele makes me happy too 

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:53.233
Ukulele’s such a cute little, cute little instrument. I love it.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.653
Should we try the opposite? Sadness?

00:03:56.986 --> 00:03:57.987
Let’s do it.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.198
Alright, K. Sadness. Here we go.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.709
You guys here the difference? Quite different from happiness.

00:04:52.709 --> 00:04:56.713
It’s a little bit slower. And there’s some sad chords in there too, right?

00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:58.047
Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:58.256 --> 00:05:02.093
You know sometimes it’s totally fine to be sad. It’s just, that’s what we do as human beings.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.305
If we have, if we don’t have sadness, how do we know we’re happy? Right?

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:13.146
Every feeling you have, um, is just important as the other. So, um, it’s okay to feel, um, any of those feelings.

00:05:13.688 --> 00:05:17.108
I’ve got an idea for the next one. How about excitement?

00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:20.194
I need some excitement. Good idea. Let’s try that.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:42.842
That was pretty exciting. That’s…That’s how excitement should feel.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:48.097
Sometimes excitement is hard because, uh, it’s really fast, so you have to kind of keep up with the music.

00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:49.682
So you’re kind of running along with it.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.309
That’s a big, that’s a big challenge for me.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:54.187
I almost dropped my instruments sometimes, playing excitement.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:59.734
I have dropped my instruments sometimes from excitement. So that’s, that’s the danger of being too excited about playing.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:00.735
Yeah.

00:06:00.735 --> 00:06:03.738
So for our last one, how about if we try calmness?

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:07.200
Okay, that would be a good one. Yeah, I need to calm down here.

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:57.792
That was a lot of fun.

00:06:58.418 --> 00:06:59.710
I, I felt really calm.

00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:01.754
What about the music made you feel calm?

00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:07.385
It was like long and soft. Nothing changed very quickly. It was very slow--

00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:07.927
Yes.

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:08.928
--And smooth. Yeah.

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:15.476
It took its time and there wasn’t a big beat. And, uh, it kind of flowed.

00:07:15.476 --> 00:07:19.897
Uh, do you, do you hear that sound? Is that you, Toby?

00:07:19.897 --> 00:07:20.773
It’s not me.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:24.527
Wonder where it’s coming from. Maybe you guys should go take a look?

00:07:24.694 --> 00:07:26.404
Yeah, go check it out. Let’s see what that is.

00:07:26.487 --> 00:07:29.532
Thank you guys so much for joining us! This was great. We had a lot of fun. Bye!

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:30.867
Bye!

